# same treatment as Maia (owner I: generalise): one-joint torso, long hair + four capes.
# MEASURED, then corrected: the first pass at these numbers (700/800/800) put Gol's own hair
# permanently INSIDE his torso — the intro-cinematic leg reported evilbro resid=300 (every frame of
# the window) at 261 units deep, while Maia next to him read resid=0. A collider big enough to
# swallow the chain it is meant to deflect is not a body volume, it is a trap. Sized down to the
# same proportions that hold on Maia, and his hair used to take colskip=2: `hairBase` and `hair1` sit on
# the skull and the nape, i.e. inside the head/neck volume BY CONSTRUCTION, exactly like every other
# hair root in this file.
# `goatee` is NOT on this volume: a beard hangs off the CHIN, which is inside the head sphere by
# construction — the same reason every hair root carries colskip. Listing it here is what pinned
# evilbro at resid=300 / 261 units deep for a whole window while Maia beside him read 0.
# no flare on Gol: he wears a robe, and the orb strands hang beside a BARE leg volume.
# `sleeveL` is NOT on these: it is a cuff hanging off `Lelbow`, i.e. it WRAPS the arm — a volume
# swept along that same arm contains it by construction and can only push it out forever. The
# per-chain residual counter named it directly (evilbro chain 9, 900 frames); before that counter
# existed this was three build cycles of guessing at radii. Same class as the goatee on the head
# volume and the orb strands in the pelvis volume.
